> How far down are Sokoban & Minetown? I usually try to keep DL & XL
> about the same - is this a reasonable approach, or am I descending too
> slowly? 

A lot depends on the character you are playing. My current character is a 
dwarvish archaeologist, which means that gnomes and dwarves are generally 
peaceful. So the route for this game was to go straight to minetown to see 
the priest while still at XL1, then back to the main dungeon level 
(remember you DONT have to do all of the gnomish mines branch in one go) 
and down to Sokoban. By the time I got back up from minetown my pet was 
chunky enough to be killing most things, so I just kept it nearby on my way 
down to sokoban. I completed sokoban then went back to do the rest of the 
mines. Now I'm back descending the main dungeon.

With a character that isn't a candidate for the protection racket, I would 
probably do Sokoban first, then minetown, then possibly some more of the 
main dungeon before doing the rest of the mines, but a lot depends on the 
top level of the mines. If the mine levels are lit I'm much more likely to 
venture in with a low level character than if they are dark.

I don't really look at experience level at all when descending, I tend to 
explore each level to fill out the map, then descend.

Of course, I may not be a good model to follow, I've only ascended once, 
and my last good candidate for an ascension died on DL forty-something 
after accidentally biting a cockatrice (he was a vampire lord at the time).

